      "action": "Authorize format access per requesting client.",
      "mechanism": "Server-side capability checks, not the flag alone, determine creation and opening eligibility.",
      "implementation": "Require enabled creation flag plus declared write capability; require declared read capability for opening. Revalidate session declarations rather than trusting cached account capabilities.",
      "check": "Seed a capable account cache, then connect an old client: new-format creation and opening fail; authorized legacy reads succeed.",
      "risk": "Incorrect declarations remain possible; fail closed only for new-format operations."
